From d6308e46eed6d87a8217e7c4c1a96fed9deb0713 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rime-fork <rime-fork@localhost>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:30:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Settings window: a reading page; a first-run guide
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A new 讀音 page picks which reading of a character comes first (librime patch 0010: 蓬萊音, 中州音, 兼收並蓄). A click sets the schema options on the sessions that are open (like the F4 menu) and writes "switches/@N/reset" into the schema's custom file, then deploys, so new sessions follow it. Search finds it under 讀音, 中州, 兼收.

The store no longer treats a list append ("switches/+") as blocking keys that name an existing item by number (switches/@3/reset).

The first time a text field uses Sable, a small window asks for the reading (蓬萊音 or 中州音). The choice goes through the same model as the settings window; pages seen are recorded in penglai-onboarding.json in the user folder, so it shows once. More pages can be added later. `Sable --onboarding --user-dir DIR` runs it on a sandbox.
---
